From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Son Luong Ngoc <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:38:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nfsserve: harden writable loopback exports

Writable NFS projections need mutation checks and replay behavior that
do not lose acknowledged changes or repeat completed requests. Forward
directory cookies and exclusive-create verifiers, distinguish file and
directory removal, and delegate guarded mutations to atomic filesystem
callbacks.  Reject directory buffers too small for the first entry.

Bound record decoding, allocations, connections and globally
admitted RPCs.  Keep response forwarding independent of request
backpressure. Cache completed replies within a bounded replay window,
release failed parsing reservations, and allow retryable JUKEBOX
responses to run again rather than become sticky failures. Filesystems
can raise bounded admission to reserve metadata capacity while lazy
content waits.

Filesystem implementations must provide the new guarded-mutation
and rmdir callbacks and accept the exclusive-create verifier and
directory cookie.  This remains a single-user loopback transport,
not an authenticated NFS service or a distributed lock manager.
